{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T10:40:27.090Z","ordinal":15462,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a125af-5d46-7871-9bed-a128df2c2957","turn_id":"01a12fa1-890e-7f90-887f-d6c42cc85d6b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-069fe739-5e6e-452c-afaa-03fc8413cf2e","process_id":"49998","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr create --base main --head ao/neatlogs-hack-5/comparison-evidence-input --title 'Report matched baseline, prior and trace-history comparison passes' --body '## Summary\n- Adds --comparison-dir for measured plan signals and explicit A/B/C run-path assignments (optional --comparison-passes JSON elsewhere keeps source signals read-only).\n- Exactly A top-tier baseline, B Tally v1/priors, C Tally v2/trace-history: task-level cost/verdict/attempts, pass-level cost/pass rate/attempts, three SVG charts and per-pass size-cost correlations.\n- Joins only at the exact pinned base SHA and recorded task text; unknown/wrong pass, missing base/text, dry/active runs are excluded. Missing passes/tasks remain pending; skipped/interrupted results retain denominators.\n- Raw decision provenance remains in CSV/JSON. Observed routing statistics need not imply a learned P90 cap; C label alone is not proof history changed every decision.\n- Records actual capped-stop/escalation evidence separately from the benchmark.\n\n## Validation\n805 tests pass on main 9f18111, typecheck/build clean. Fake tests cover missing data, base/text mismatches, A/B/C isolation, simulated/active exclusion, duplicates and skipped outcomes. Three charts visually checked via AO; no console errors. Cached regeneration makes no API calls.\n\n## Live read-only evidence\nReal cap retry run-20261012-100856Z: cheap stopped at $0.01956044 against $0.018 cap, middle passed at $0.16957640; total $0.18913684. Fresh readback verifies both stored worker traces (12/12 across audited runs), 6 history-cost matches. Failure classification stays ceiling/ledger; trace delivery does not retroactively make it trace-derived.\n\n## Limits / next data\nA/B/C costs currently pending; no invented savings or paid comparison results. Awaiting lane A paths. Plan: five tasks at base 565e6ccd757ff794ead643dac7359efe67ec9db2, BENCH-1 dependents/graph unmeasured; single repo/repeat, repeated tasks not independent, model pricing/setup/caching confounded. Cost remains list-price/AO estimate, not invoice. No paid workers or cfo.ai writes.\nReport: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/report.md' "],"cwd":"file:///Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/worktrees/neatlogs-hack/neatlogs-hack-5","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr create --base main --head ao/neatlogs-hack-5/comparison-evidence-input --title 'Report matched baseline, prior and trace-history comparison passes' --body '## Summary\n- Adds --comparison-dir for measured plan signals and explicit A/B/C run-path assignments (optional --comparison-passes JSON elsewhere keeps source signals read-only).\n- Exactly A top-tier baseline, B Tally v1/priors, C Tally v2/trace-history: task-level cost/verdict/attempts, pass-level cost/pass rate/attempts, three SVG charts and per-pass size-cost correlations.\n- Joins only at the exact pinned base SHA and recorded task text; unknown/wrong pass, missing base/text, dry/active runs are excluded. Missing passes/tasks remain pending; skipped/interrupted results retain denominators.\n- Raw decision provenance remains in CSV/JSON. Observed routing statistics need not imply a learned P90 cap; C label alone is not proof history changed every decision.\n- Records actual capped-stop/escalation evidence separately from the benchmark.\n\n## Validation\n805 tests pass on main 9f18111, typecheck/build clean. Fake tests cover missing data, base/text mismatches, A/B/C isolation, simulated/active exclusion, duplicates and skipped outcomes. Three charts visually checked via AO; no console errors. Cached regeneration makes no API calls.\n\n## Live read-only evidence\nReal cap retry run-20261012-100856Z: cheap stopped at $0.01956044 against $0.018 cap, middle passed at $0.16957640; total $0.18913684. Fresh readback verifies both stored worker traces (12/12 across audited runs), 6 history-cost matches. Failure classification stays ceiling/ledger; trace delivery does not retroactively make it trace-derived.\n\n## Limits / next data\nA/B/C costs currently pending; no invented savings or paid comparison results. Awaiting lane A paths. Plan: five tasks at base 565e6ccd757ff794ead643dac7359efe67ec9db2, BENCH-1 dependents/graph unmeasured; single repo/repeat, repeated tasks not independent, model pricing/setup/caching confounded. Cost remains list-price/AO estimate, not invoice. No paid workers or cfo.ai writes.\nReport: /Users/vaibhaav/.ao/data/artifacts/neatlogs-hack-5/routing-evidence/report.md' "}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/145\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/145\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":149011083},"formatted_output":"https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/145\n"},"started_at_ms":1791801623940,"completed_at_ms":1791801627090}}
